    \item[2] Simplify each part of the inequality.
    \item[3] Solve the inequality for $x$.
\end{itemize}

Here's the solution:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item[1] Multiplying each part of the inequality by 35:
    $$ \frac{2}{3} \cdot 35 < \frac{x}{5} \cdot 35 < \frac{6}{7} \cdot 35 $$
    $$ \frac{70}{3} < 7x < 30 $$

    \item[2] Simplifying each part of the inequality:
    $$ \frac{70}{3} < 7x < 30 $$
    Dividing each part by 7:
    $$ \frac{70}{3 \cdot 7} < x < \frac{30}{7} $$
    $$ \frac{10}{3} < x < \frac{30}{7} $$
    Approximately,
    $$ 3.333... < x < 4.2857... $$

    \item[3] Since $x$ must be an integer, the possible values of $x$ are 4.
\end{enumerate}

Therefore, $x = 4$.

