completions_8:
\begin{align*} \label{eq:1} \text{Number of ways to pick 3 boys from 7} &= \binom{7}{3} = \frac{7!}{3!(7-3)!} = \frac{7!}{3!4!} = \frac{7 \times 6 \times 5}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 35 \\ \text{Number of ways to pick 2 girls from 4} &= \binom{4}{2} = \frac{4!}{2!(4-2)!} = \frac{4!}{2!2!} = \frac{4 \times 3}{2 \times 1} = 6 \end{align*} 
Therefore, the total number of ways to pick 3 boys and 2 girls is 
$$ \binom{7}{3} \times \binom{4}{2} = 35 \times 6 = 210 $$
\boxed{210}
