Substituting the second equation into the first, we get:
\begin{align*} \frac{2}{5} N + N &= 35 \\ \frac{2N + 5N}{5} &= 35 \\ \frac{7N}{5} &= 35 \\ 7N &= 35 \times 5 \\ 7N &= 175 \\ N &= \frac{175}{7} \\ N &= 25 \end{align*}
Then, $L = \frac{2}{5} N = \frac{2}{5} (25) = 2 \times 5 = 10$.

