    \item Combining these two equations, we get $f(x) = -f(x)$. This implies $2f(x) = 0$, so $f(x) = 0$ for all $x$ in its domain.
    \item Therefore, the only function that is both even and odd is the zero function, $f(x) = 0$.
    \item The number of functions that are both even and odd is 1.
