Combining these two equations, we have $f(x) = -f(x)$, which implies $2f(x) = 0$.
Therefore, $f(x) = 0$ for all $x$ in the domain.

The only function that is both even and odd is the zero function, $f(x) = 0$.
Thus, the number of functions that are both even and odd is 1.

